STATEMENT: >>>
First whole-canon render of the view organization, 2026-08-30, from a
fresh export of the worktree at commit 44493bce plus the uncommitted
migration, backend, renderer and task work. The payload, schema
whiteboard-view/2: 4 roots (NAR-CANON, NAR-MECHANISM-MOOD-REVIEW,
NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER, NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW), 72 narratives, 329 nodes, 831
edges, 476 rows of which 117 carry a reference line (279 references in
all) and 145 a source line; backlinks on 220 nodes; 16 widget words in
use. Checks on that export: sdoc check 329 nodes, 0 findings; fp-check
491 entries, 491 never signed, 0 suspect; cycle-check 757 role-carrying
edges, 0 cycles; file-check 0 findings; view-check 7 findings, every one
cited-node-superseded and pre-existing (three citations of
DEC-NODE-TYPE-GRID under the semantic layer, four of
DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE and DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA under the
whiteboard view), 0 canon-wide. Page sizes: canon.html 1,560,146 bytes,
canon.artifact.html 1,559,991 bytes, canon.json 1,973,933 bytes -- a tenth
of the artifact cap. Task timings, warm: view:render 2.77 s and 2.45 s
wall (export, four per-root checks, wireline, two renders); view:serve
answered canon.html with HTTP 200 on 127.0.0.1:8791 and stopped cleanly.
Screenshots at 390 px in both themes, 22 screens (the canon's Start,
Types, Edges, Words, Whiteboards; the semantic layer's Start, Types, a
type, Edges, Topics, a topic with a word preselected, Gaps, a gap, Words,
Sheet; the whiteboard view's Start and data model; a node; Nodes; and the
canon's Start, Edges and Nodes with whiteboard switched off), compared
screen by screen against the v1 page's 82-element inventory.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
What the comparison changed, all in docs/sdoc/view/template.html and the
canon, none in the backend: the top tab strip clamps a label to two lines
at 9rem instead of one line at 14rem, so a root's title reads instead of
ellipsizing at its fourth word; the sub strip is tighter so seven one-word
tabs fit a phone; tables drop to 0.82rem under 480 px so the live-count
column stays in view; the edges figure spaces its boxes wider and tries
more label positions; a tab whose data is narratives, and a root other
than the canon's, leave the strip when their system is off, and a route
into a switched-off root lands on a note; a glossary tagged with a query
word draws the backend's computed table (the canon's Words tab drew "no
terms" before). In the canon: PLACE on the whiteboard-view and mood-review
children (legend card, screens, an Edges tab retitled Edges), and a strip
section under the semantic layer's Topics tab for v1's rows-by-topic bar.
Left alone: the seven cited-node-superseded findings (the sheet is a
snapshot, re-cut rather than edited), the semantic layer's edges figure,
which still overlaps labels among six types at 390 px and scrolls, and the
systems table's meaning column, which scrolls off a phone.
<<<
